== Trivia ==
* This item makes Isaac resemble {{E|Uriel}} and {{E|Gabriel}}, and its ability resembles the two angels' abilities to fire a directed holy blast.
* This item may be a reference to the [[fireemblem:Seraph Robe|Seraph Robe]] from the [[wikipedia:Fire Emblem|Fire Emblem]] video game series, which shared a similar sprite in previous installments of the game.
* Isaac's glowing eyes with the item may be a reference to Moses in the Book of Exodus. Chapter 34 details how, after he received another set of stone tablets with the Ten Commandments from God, Moses's face started shining and became difficult to look at. Henceforth, Moses would only show his face when revealing what God had told him.
* [[anti:Revelation|Revelation]] originates from the ''Antibirth'' mod. This item is significantly different from its ''Antibirth'' counterpart, which gave stats up and a spectral {{t|Brain Worm}} effect to Isaac's tears. It also gave Isaac two immortal hearts instead of soul hearts, which was a [[Hearts|heart pickup]] that was never transferred to ''Repentance''.

== Bugs ==
{{bug|When combined with {{I|Chocolate Milk}}, {{I|Cursed Eye}}, {{I|Monstro's Lung}}, or {{I|Tech X}}, releasing a Revelation attack may prevent a charged shot from firing at the same time as expected. The charged shot is delayed by about ~0.5 seconds. Holding a full charge for a longer time makes the delay more likely to happen.}}

